Translation patch: <RistrettoPoint as Sum<T>>::sum (src/ristretto.rs)

Change: `iter.fold(RistrettoPoint::identity(), |acc, item| acc + item.borrow())` becomes a `while let`
loop accumulating `acc = acc + item.borrow()`.

Why: the Aeneas Lean library models only `Iterator::next`; the provided
methods (`map`, `zip`, `fold`, `filter`, `collect`, `rev`/`skip` on adapters, ...)
are missing (AeneasVerif/aeneas#1057), so the original does not build in Lean.

Behaviour: identical: `fold` is defined as exactly this loop over `next()`.

Remove this patch when Aeneas translates the original code: delete the file,
run ./scripts/aeneas-translate.sh and `lake build`, and check both succeed.

diff --git a/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs b/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
index 269662d..f95d62b 100644
--- a/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
+++ b/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
@@ -883,11 +883,15 @@ impl<T> Sum<T> for RistrettoPoint
 where
     T: Borrow<RistrettoPoint>,
 {
-    fn sum<I>(iter: I) -> Self
+    fn sum<I>(mut iter: I) -> Self
     where
         I: Iterator<Item = T>,
     {
-        iter.fold(RistrettoPoint::identity(), |acc, item| acc + item.borrow())
+        let mut acc = RistrettoPoint::identity();
+        while let Some(item) = iter.next() {
+            acc = acc + item.borrow();
+        }
+        acc
     }
 }
 
